    caidasPreviasTitulo: "Prior drop measurement",
    caidasPreviasDesc: "For each stock selected by \"low flow\" (and by regular \"flow\", as a reference), did it come from a recent price drop? For each threshold (5%, 10%, 15%, 20%), it looks for how many sessions back you need to go to find a price at least that % higher than the one on the selection day — the most recent point from which today's price already represents that drop, exploring up to 60 sessions back. This check alone doesn't distinguish between the two remaining hypotheses (the technical one and the \"boring\" one: both predict a drop happened) — that's what \"Prior volume profile\", this tool's companion, is for — but it confirms or rules out whether the price pattern actually exists.",
    caidasPreviasBotonCargando: "Measuring prior drops...",
    caidasPreviasBoton: "Measure prior drops",
    colUmbralCaida: "Drop threshold",
    colPctAlcanzado: "% reaching it",
    colSesionesAtras: "Sessions back (avg)",

    perfilVolumenTitulo: "Prior volume profile",
    perfilVolumenDesc: "The companion to \"Prior drop measurement\", and the check that actually separates the two remaining hypotheses. If a stock comes from a price drop, did that drop come with a sharp one-day volume spike (everyone selling at once, the typical signature of a real crash — favors the hypothesis that \"low flow\" simply mechanically avoids recent crashes) or with low, sustained volume, with no spike at all (more consistent with a quiet accumulation phase)? For each selection, the previous 20 sessions are examined and the ratio between the single highest day's volume and the average volume over that stretch is calculated — a ratio well above 1 (over 2.5×) indicates a clear spike; close to 1 means sustained volume with no standout day.",
    perfilVolumenBotonCargando: "Calculating volume profile...",
    perfilVolumenBoton: "Calculate prior volume profile",
    colSelecciones: "Selections",
    colPicoRatioMedio: "Peak/avg ratio (mean)",
    colPctConPico: "% with volume spike",
    colPctSinPico: "% without spike (sustained)",

    rentFlujoBajoTitulo: "Low money flow selection returns",
    rentFlujoBajoDesc: "Straight to the variable that actually matters (returns), instead of continuing to look at intermediate variables (price, volume) that were already thinning out as the signal got smoothed — the same logic as a moving average: the longer the window, the more any short signal gets flattened out. Goes through, for each marked index, every combination of averaged sessions (2, 3 and 4) and backtest duration (20, 50 and 120 sessions), always with the \"low flow\" method, with 6 non-overlapping repetitions per combination. Scope deliberately reduced compared to other tools in this section: downloading and processing several indices at once, with every combination, is the heaviest check in the whole app — only mark the indices you want to check on each run.",
    rentFlujoBajoEtiquetaSeleccion: "Indices to include:",
    rentFlujoBajoBotonCargando: "Calculating (may take a while)...",
    rentFlujoBajoBoton: "Calculate low flow returns",
    sesionesPromediadasEtiqueta: "Averaged sessions",
    colRentCarteraRango: "Portfolio return (range)",
    colRentIndiceMediaSimple: "Index return (average)",
    repeticionesInsuficientesAviso: "fewer than the 6 requested, less reliable",
    colDistanciaInferior: "Distance to index (lower end)",
    colDistanciaSuperior: "Distance to index (upper end)",
    top3RentabilidadRealTitulo: (duracion) => `The 3 most chosen stocks at this duration — actual return of today vs. ${duracion} sessions ago:`,
    colRentabilidadRealTicker: "Return (today vs. N sessions ago)",
    factorOptimoEtiqueta: "Optimal (currently configured)",
